Incorrect selections: <<if $badList1 neq "">><<print $badList1>><<else>>None<</if>>

Methionine is often the first limiting amino acid in grain based poultry diets because cereal proteins contain relatively low methionine concentrations. Adequate methionine is required for protein synthesis and methyl group metabolism. Lysine can also become limiting but is commonly second. Leucine and histidine are not usually the primary limitation in grain-fed chickens. The issue reflects amino acid balance rather than energy metabolism.

