:: F2 {"position":"525,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: C. Their synthesis requires inputs from both glycolysis and the pentose phosphate pathway

You correctly identified <<print $corr2>> of 1 correct answers.<br>
You missed <<print $miss2>> correct answers.<br>
You selected <<print $bad2>> incorrect answers.

Missed correct answers: <<if $missList2 neq "">><<print $missList2>><<else>>None<</if>><br>
Incorrect selections: <<if $badList2 neq "">><<print $badList2>><<else>>None<</if>>

Aromatic amino acids arise through pathways that draw carbon from glycolysis and the pentose phosphate pathway. Their biosynthesis therefore requires substantial precursor investment and metabolic coordination. They are not confined to mitochondria, do not specifically depend on ATP from fatty acid oxidation, and are not called expensive simply because plants synthesise them. The shikimate pathway integrates central carbon metabolism to generate aromatic structures.

[[Continue->Q3]]


:: F3 {"position":"775,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: A. Alanine

You correctly identified <<print $corr3>> of 1 correct answers.<br>
You missed <<print $miss3>> correct answers.<br>
You selected <<print $bad3>> incorrect answers.

Missed correct answers: <<if $missList3 neq "">><<print $missList3>><<else>>None<</if>><br>
Incorrect selections: <<if $badList3 neq "">><<print $badList3>><<else>>None<</if>>

Alanine is directly connected to pyruvate by alanine aminotransferase. Transamination readily interconverts these compounds and links amino acid and carbohydrate metabolism. Glutamate is more closely related to α-ketoglutarate, while aspartate is linked to oxaloacetate. Histidine follows a different biosynthetic and catabolic route. This reaction helps redistribute nitrogen while maintaining carbon skeleton flow between pathways.

[[Continue->Q4]]


:: F4 {"position":"1025,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: D. It cannot be synthesised by the organism and must be obtained from food

You correctly identified <<print $corr4>> of 1 correct answers.<br>
You missed <<print $miss4>> correct answers.<br>
